<?xml version="1.0"?>
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Config:etc/system_file.xsd">
    <system>
        <!-- Declared here too: other Slova modules may declare the same tab; Magento
             merges identical ids, and this module must not depend on any of them. -->
        <tab id="slova" translate="label" sortOrder="400">
            <label>Slova</label>
        </tab>
        <!-- Every comment is on ONE line: Magento translates it by its exact text,
             so line breaks and indentation would have to be repeated in i18n/*.csv. -->
        <section id="slova_cookieconsent" translate="label" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
            <label>Cookie Consent</label>
            <tab>slova</tab>
            <resource>Slova_CookieConsent::config</resource>

            <group id="general" translate="label" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>General</label>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Enable Cookie Consent</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>This banner replaces Magento's Cookie Restriction Mode and hides its notice. Set Stores > Configuration > General > Web > Default Cookie Settings > Cookie Restriction Mode to No.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="categories" translate="label comment" type="multiselect" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Optional Categories</label>
                    <source_model>Slova\CookieConsent\Model\Config\Source\OptionalCategories</source_model>
                    <comment>The categories visitors can switch on or off. Necessary is always listed and always on. Offer only the categories your store really uses.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="privacy_page" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Privacy Policy Link</label>
                    <comment>The URL key of a CMS page (for example privacy-policy) or a full URL starting with https://. Leave empty to show no link.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="consent_version" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Consent Version</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <comment>Raise this number after you change your cookie policy or add a category: every visitor is asked again.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="lifetime_days" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="50" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Remember the Choice For (Days)</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <comment>After this many days the banner asks again. 180 days (about six months) follows the French CNIL; most EU regulators accept up to 13 months.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="reopen_button" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="60" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Floating Settings Button</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment><![CDATA[A small button in the corner that reopens the preferences once a choice is made. Withdrawing consent must be as easy as giving it: if you turn this off, add a link to <code>#cookie-settings</code> to every page (for example in the footer).]]></comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
            </group>

            <group id="content" translate="label comment" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Texts</label>
                <comment>Leave a field empty to use the built-in text, translated into the store view's language.</comment>
                <field id="title" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Banner Title</label>
                </field>
                <field id="message" translate="label" type="textarea" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Banner Message</label>
                </field>
                <field id="link_label" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Privacy Policy Link Text</label>
                </field>
            </group>

            <group id="appearance" translate="label" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Appearance</label>
                <field id="position" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Banner Position</label>
                    <source_model>Slova\CookieConsent\Model\Config\Source\Position</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="accent_color" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Accent Color</label>
                    <comment>Buttons, links and switches, as a hex color such as #1d4ed8. Leave empty (or enter anything else) to follow the theme's primary color.</comment>
                </field>
            </group>

            <group id="consent_mode" translate="label" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Google Consent Mode v2</label>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Send Google Consent Mode</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>At the top of every page, before any Google tag: everything denied by default, then updated from the visitor's choice. Turn off only if your Google Tag Manager container or another module already sends the consent defaults.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="wait_for_update" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Wait for Update (ms)</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits</validate>
                    <comment>How long Google tags wait for the visitor's stored choice before they fire. 500 is Google's recommendation.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="ads_data_redaction" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Redact Ads Data Without Consent</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>While marketing consent is missing, Google Ads tags drop ad click identifiers from their requests.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
    </system>
</config>
